It depends! e.g.
1) plotting times series then CIs are useful
2) fitting SRR, variances of S&  R should be useful
3) ratio of current F&  SSB to ref pts, you need the covariances etc.

FLQuantPoint was simply designed to make FLQuant objects take up less space, i.e. if you have 1000 iterations you could condense it down to mean, variance,...
But if you are not running Monte Carlo simulations then FLQuantPoint is not needed.

Laurie





